            <ArticleTitle>Long-term patient-controlled analgesia in children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>941-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three children who received patient-controlled analgesia for periods of up to 41 days are described. In each case patient-controlled analgesia allowed pain control to be achieved in difficult situations. No patient developed tolerance or clinical signs of dependence. This use of long-term patient-controlled analgesia warrants further evaluation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
